From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:35:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 144/342] MediaPlayer: NV12 overlays, decoded into the overlay
 bitmaps

Where the overlay can't show B_RGB32, MediaPlayer now asks the decoder
for B_NV12 first, then B_YCbCr422 as before; frame sizes, black frames
and the name table know B_NV12.

And the decoder now writes into the overlay bitmaps when their areas can
be cloned (meson_hdmi's can): the consumer's shared buffer group was left
out for overlays (a TODO about mapping overlay bitmaps into BBuffers), so
every frame was copied once more, into the bitmap. On the ODROID-C2, 1080p60
HEVC takes 9% of the CPU instead of 25%, H.264 7% instead of 14%, with every
frame shown and no tearing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
